Version 2.0 had 684 deposits, after the addition of 25 new deposits.

Additional information was added to resources and production fields as needed.

The deposit table was updated in 2026 (ver. 3) to include 592 new deposits in addition to updating 248 previous entries. Critical minerals have been updated to include those on the 2025 U.S. critical minerals list.

2025 critical minerals list - https://www.usgs.gov/news/science-snippet/interior-department-releases-final-2025-list-critical-minerals.

Below is a list of changes:

The following were added:
592 deposits were added to the version 2.0 list.

The following were modified:
248 deposits were modified to include the critical minerals added in 2025 or other changes, like those listed below.

The following are the name changes:

Arctic changed to Arctic (Upper Kobuk Mineral Projects)
Aspen mine changed to Smuggler;
